; datomic: the pure-data dialect on protos. Its types, and what they bear.
; Potential<T> is generic and Site, Positions and Variant are borrowed reader
; handles: none has a Declaration form. Protos's String-backed scalar wrappers
; (Symbol, Word, Opaque and Text) are imported names without a Declaration
; storage form; their omission is deliberate rather than a false Text shape.
; DatomWord is a validated private-field wrapper. Ethos has no opaque-newtype
; declaration form, so it is imported from this crate rather than falsely
; declared as an alias of Word.
; The generic bearers of Datomic (Vector, Option, Result, Box of a Datomic) have no association form.
Types
[ protos:[ BareRefusal Integer Extent Path Separator Enclosure Boundary StructuralProblem.Problem StructuralFault.Fault Symbol Word Opaque Text Textualizable Protosizable Conceivable ]
  crate:[ Datomic Worded DatomWord ] ]
[ Datom.[ Variant.{ Symbol Datom } Struct.Vector<Datom> Vector.Vector<Datom> Text.Text Meaning.Opaque Word.DatomWord ]
  WordRefusal.[ Bare.BareRefusal Period.Word ]
